971.solution_latex:
Write $Y = AX$ where

$$
A = \begin{pmatrix} 1 & 2 & -1 \\ 2 & -1 & 1 \end{pmatrix}.
$$

(a) The mean vector of $Y$ is


$$
E(Y) = A\mu = \begin{pmatrix} 1 & 2 & -1 \\ 2 & -1 & 1 \end{pmatrix}
 \begin{pmatrix} 1 \\ 2 \\ 3 \end{pmatrix}
 = \begin{pmatrix} 1(1)+2(2)-1(3) \\ 2(1)-1(2)+1(3) \end{pmatrix}
 = \begin{pmatrix} 2 \\ 3 \end{pmatrix}.
$$

(b) The variance-covariance matrix of $Y$ is $\operatorname{Var}(Y) = A\Sigma A'$. First compute


$$
A\Sigma = \begin{pmatrix} 1 & 2 & -1 \\ 2 & -1 & 1 \end{pmatrix}
 \begin{pmatrix} 4 & 1 & 0 \\ 1 & 9 & 2 \\ 0 & 2 & 16 \end{pmatrix}
 = \begin{pmatrix} 6 & 17 & -12 \\ 7 & -5 & 14 \end{pmatrix}.
$$

 Then


$$
A\Sigma A' = \begin{pmatrix} 6 & 17 & -12 \\ 7 & -5 & 14 \end{pmatrix}
 \begin{pmatrix} 1 & 2 \\ 2 & -1 \\ -1 & 1 \end{pmatrix}
 = \begin{pmatrix} 52 & -17 \\ -17 & 235 \end{pmatrix}.
$$

 Thus $\operatorname{Var}(Y_1)=52$, $\operatorname{Var}(Y_2)=235$, and $\operatorname{Cov}(Y_1,Y_2)=-17$.
(c) The correlation coefficient is


$$
r_{Y_1Y_2} = \frac{\operatorname{Cov}(Y_1,Y_2)}{\sqrt{\operatorname{Var}(Y_1)\,\operatorname{Var}(Y_2)}}
 = \frac{-17}{\sqrt{52 \cdot 235}}
 = \frac{-17}{\sqrt{12220}}
 \approx -0.154.
$$

 The value is negative and close to zero, indicating a weak negative linear relationship between $Y_1$ and $Y_2$.

